0 A hand pump, a two-port pneumatic cylinder and a lever valve are connected by three looping hoses.
0 Name: TECHNIC_PNEUMATIC_HOSE-Constraints.ldr
0 Author: Holly Wood
0 Unofficial Model
0 // Scene: Two tall cylinders stand beside a low valve on a small perforated-brick support. Blue, yellow and brown hoses make the connections visible; straight tube samples and a loose ring sit separately in front.
0 // Rigid construction: 2797c01 is the hand pump, 2793c01 the two-port cylinder and 4694c01 the valve. Technic bricks and friction pins provide part of the mounting context.
0 // Build lesson: Build a pneumatic machine around accessible controls, the cylinder mounting points and the actual nozzles. Deliberate hose routes can make the air system readable without hiding the mechanism.
0 // Reuse: The arrangement demonstrates components and routing, not a supported working machine. Preserve pump/valve access, verify each nozzle and cylinder stroke, and separate the loose tube samples from the functional assembly.
0 ROTATION CENTER 0 0 0 1 "CUSTOM" 
0 ROTATION CONFIG 0 0
